<article class="env-example" id="05CW">
<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/05CW">Example <span data-tag="05CW">4.8.7.7</span>.</a> Let $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ be an $\infty $-category and let $n$ be an integer. Then the projection map $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}\rightarrow \Delta ^0$ factors as a composition </p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}\xrightarrow {F'} \operatorname {h}_{\mathit{\leq {}n-1}}{\mathit{(\operatorname{\mathcal{C}})}} \xrightarrow {G} \Delta ^0, \]
</div>
<p> where $\operatorname {h}_{\mathit{\leq {}n-1}}{\mathit{(\operatorname{\mathcal{C}})}}$ is the homotopy $(n-1)$-category constructed in §<a data-tag="0596" href="/tag/0596">4.7.9</a>. This factorization satisfies the requirements of Theorem <a data-tag="05CS" href="/tag/05CS">4.8.7.3</a>. Assume for simplicity that $n \geq 0$ (for $n &lt; 0$ the result follows from Example <a data-tag="05CT" href="/tag/05CT">4.8.7.4</a>). Then the functor $G$ is $n$-faithful because $\operatorname {h}_{\mathit{\leq {}n-1}}{\mathit{(\operatorname{\mathcal{C}})}}$ is locally $(n-2)$-truncated (Example <a data-tag="05AZ" href="/tag/05AZ">4.8.3.14</a>), and the functor $F'$ is categorically $n$-connective by Example <a data-tag="05A7" href="/tag/05A7">4.8.5.19</a>. </p>
</article>
